From: ftcommunity-TXT <dev@ftcommunity.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:56:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Reset SIGINT and SIGTERM dispositions at startup

When started in the background by a shell (e.g.
`sudo /usr/bin/ft_bt_remote_start.sh &` in the GUI app), POSIX sh sets
SIGINT and SIGQUIT to SIG_IGN. Reset SIGINT and SIGTERM to SIG_DFL at
the beginning of main() so `pkill -SIGINT ft_bt_remote_se` and signalfd
can terminate the server cleanly.
---
 src/ft_bt_remote_server.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ft_bt_remote_server.c b/src/ft_bt_remote_server.c
index 2222222..3333333 100644
--- a/src/ft_bt_remote_server.c
+++ b/src/ft_bt_remote_server.c
@@ -906,6 +906,9 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 	int opt;
 	sigset_t mask;
 
+	signal(SIGINT, SIG_DFL);
+	signal(SIGTERM, SIG_DFL);
+
 	struct server server;
 	memset(&server, 0, sizeof(server));
 	
